# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Anything not matched here falls through to
# the SPA (Vite-built `dist/` served from the project root).
#
# Status 200 means rewrite (proxy) — the URL in the browser stays as
# wallpaperexchange.com/... while the bytes come from the backend. Search
# engines see the SEO content under the apex domain, which is what we want.

/api/*         https://api.wallpaperexchange.com/api/:splat    200
/sitemap.xml   https://api.wallpaperexchange.com/sitemap.xml   200
/robots.txt    https://api.wallpaperexchange.com/robots.txt    200

# OG / Twitter prerender for bots that don't run JS. The CF Pages catch-all
# normally returns the SPA HTML, but for /wallpaper/:slug we want bots to get
# the meta-rich backend prerender. CF Pages can't do User-Agent matching in
# _redirects, so we just always rewrite — the rendered HTML still works fine
# in real browsers (links to / and to /wallpaper/:slug all point back to the
# SPA), and the SPA hydrates as soon as JS runs anywhere it's loaded.
#
# (Disabled by default — uncomment once tested. Without it, social shares
# still degrade gracefully to the SPA index.html.)
# /wallpaper/:slug  https://api.wallpaperexchange.com/__og/wallpaper/:slug  200
